  npm test,test/history-provenance-correction.test.ts,project,1200,pi-agent,"2026-08-28T21:14:14.324Z",local_mutation,fix/refuse-unattested-publish-fallback,history prefix preservation regression
close_reason: "Root cause was in the tokeniser, not the verifier: tokenizeCommands treated the '{' of a parameter expansion as a brace-group separator, so ${missing[0]} split into '$', 'missing[0]' and 'publish' and the command word the fail-closed check looks for never existed. Taught the tokeniser that ${...} is one word (matching the existing $( ... ) case), which also stops a publish reaching the shell through an expansion from being read as a different command. Narrowed INDEXED_ARRAY_EXPRESSION to numeric indices so the whole-array forms ${name[@]}/${name[*]}, which the evaluator path already re-scans, are not reported twice. Split expandArrays into two single-group passes, removing an unreachable 'allName ?? \"\"' branch instead of leaving coverage at 99.52%. Evidence: 379 tests pass; each new test observed failing before its fix and passing after; coverage 100/100/100/100 via npm run coverage; npm run release:check passes end to end; ./node_modules/.bin/pm health --strict-exit exits 0 (pinned binary 2026.8.24, 4 advisory provenance warnings)."
body: ""
